content.content:
# Modular Planters

An addon for Agritech: Evolved that replaces many Advanced Planters with a few multiblocks. A block of N growing seeds produces, draws power and costs about what N Advanced Planters would.

## Language

### The multiblock

**Multiblock**:
A Modular Planter Core together with every part connected to it face to face, directly or through other parts. Diagonal contact does not connect.
_Avoid_: structure, machine

**Formed**:
A multiblock that meets the building rules and is running. A multiblock that is not formed keeps every block's contents but grows nothing.
_Avoid_: active, assembled

**Problem**:
The reason a multiblock is not formed, such as a second Core, too many parts, or a missing required part.
_Avoid_: error

**Part**:
Any Modular Planter block that joins a multiblock, other than the Core: Power, Fertilizer, Export, Planter, ME or Frame.
_Avoid_: module, component

**Modular Planter Core**:
The block that forms the multiblock, applies the built-in cloche to every Modular Planter Block, and opens the Core screen. It stores nothing itself.
_Avoid_: Planter Core, controller

**Doorway**:
The three resources a formed Core exposes to outside connections: energy in, fertilizer in, and outputs out.
_Avoid_: port, interface

**Modular Planter Power Block**:
Stores the multiblock's energy. Several Power Blocks pool their storage, and energy cannot be extracted from them.
_Avoid_: Planter Power, capacitor

**Modular Planter Fertilizer Block**:
Stores fertilizer for every Modular Planter Block in the multiblock. Several Fertilizer Blocks pool their contents.
_Avoid_: Planter Fertilizer, import block

**Modular Planter Export Block**:
Holds harvested outputs until something pulls them out. Only the multiblock inserts into it.
_Avoid_: Planter Export, output block

**Modular Planter Block**:
Grows one seed type, up to 64 seeds, from one soil type and up to two upgrade types.
_Avoid_: Planter Block, planter

**Modular Planter ME Block**:
An optional Part, present only when AE2 is installed, that connects the multiblock to an AE2 network. A multiblock can have at most one.
_Avoid_: ME interface, Planter ME

**Modular Planter Frame**:
A Part that does nothing except connect other Parts. It counts toward the part cap.
_Avoid_: Planter Frame

### Growing

**Seed**:
Any item an Advanced Planter accepts for planting, saplings included. Each seed carries its own data, such as traits added by other mods.
# AE2 and Applied Flux stay behind MeLink

The mod must load and work with AE2, Applied Flux or both missing, and both are compile-time only dependencies. The multiblock code talks to ME only through `MeLink`, an interface with no AE2 types, and every class that touches AE2 sits in the `ae2` package, reached only behind a `ModList` loaded check. `FluxBridge` is the one class that touches Applied Flux.

The ME block's registration, item, recipe and loot table exist only when AE2 is installed, and generated data that references AE2 carries a `mod_loaded` condition. The pools and the Core can be tested with a fake `MeLink` and no AE2 on the classpath.
# Growth and structure math lives in a package with no Minecraft imports

All growth, coverage, cloche and structure math is in `logic/`, which imports nothing from `net.minecraft`, `net.neoforged`, `com.mojang` or ATE. Plain JUnit tests cover it and run with `./gradlew test`, while block entities only move items and energy, fire ATE's events and call into `logic/`. Anything that needs a world is covered by GameTests instead.

ATE's numbers reach `logic/` as a plain value object that tests can fill with ATE's defaults.
# The multiblock pauses, instead of unforming, when a part's chunk is unloaded

A build can cross a chunk border, and the player can walk away from half of it. While any part's chunk is unloaded the Core waits without unforming, every block keeps its contents and every seed keeps its progress, and nothing is lost or duplicated. Treating the missing part as a broken shape would stop the Modular Planter Blocks every time the player walked away.
package io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.blockentity;

import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.MPConfig;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.ate.AteBridge;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.block.PartBlock;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.logic.PartType;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.logic.Problem;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.logic.ScanResult;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.logic.StructureScanner;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.multiblock.DoorwayHandlers;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.multiblock.FertilizerPool;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.multiblock.MeLink;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.multiblock.MeStatus;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.multiblock.Multiblock;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.multiblock.OutputSink;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.multiblock.PowerPool;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.multiblock.TickContext;
import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.registry.MPBlockEntities;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;
import net.minecraft.core.BlockPos;
import net.minecraft.core.Direction;
import net.minecraft.server.level.ServerLevel;
import net.minecraft.world.level.Level;
import net.minecraft.world.level.block.entity.BlockEntity;
import net.minecraft.world.level.block.state.BlockState;
import net.neoforged.neoforge.transfer.ResourceHandler;
import net.neoforged.neoforge.transfer.item.ItemResource;
import org.jspecify.annotations.Nullable;

public class CoreBlockEntity extends BlockEntity {
  private static final int RESCAN_INTERVAL = 20;

  private ScanResult<BlockPos> lastScan =
      new ScanResult<>(Problem.WAITING_FOR_CHUNKS, null, Map.of());
  private @Nullable Multiblock multiblock;
  private @Nullable PowerPool power;
  private @Nullable FertilizerPool fertilizer;
  private @Nullable OutputSink outputs;
  private @Nullable MeLink me;
  private @Nullable ResourceHandler<ItemResource> items;
  private boolean dirty = true;
  private boolean poolsStale;

  public CoreBlockEntity(BlockPos pos, BlockState state) {
    super(MPBlockEntities.CORE.get(), pos, state);
  }

  public static void serverTick(Level level, BlockPos pos, BlockState state, CoreBlockEntity core) {
    if (core.dirty || (level.getGameTime() + core.tickOffset()) % RESCAN_INTERVAL == 0) {
      core.scan(level);
    }
    if (level instanceof ServerLevel serverLevel) {
      core.tickPlanters(serverLevel);
    }
  }

  // The pools are null while the core waits for an unloaded chunk, and the planters then keep their
  // progress without ticking.
  private void tickPlanters(ServerLevel level) {
    if (multiblock == null
        || power == null
        || fertilizer == null
        || outputs == null
        || !allPartsLoaded()) {
      return;
    }
    MeLink link = onlineMe();
    if (link != null) {
      power.refillFrom(link);
    }
    TickContext context =
        new TickContext(
            level, level.getRandom(), AteBridge.numbers(), power, fertilizer.budget(), outputs);
    for (BlockPos pos : multiblock.planters()) {
      if (level.getBlockEntity(pos) instanceof PlanterBlockEntity planter) {
        planter.tickFromCore(context);
      }
    }
    if (link != null && (level.getGameTime() + tickOffset()) % MPConfig.ME_INTERVAL.get() == 0) {
      outputs.moveExportsInto(link);
      fertilizer.topUpFrom(link);
    }
  }

  // This returns the link only while it is online, and a removed link counts as absent and marks
  // the pools stale so the next scan rebuilds them without it.
  private @Nullable MeLink onlineMe() {
    if (me == null) {
      return null;
    }
    if (me.isRemoved()) {
      markPoolsStale();
      return null;
    }
    return me.online() ? me : null;
  }

  // Cores spread their rescans and ME transfers over different ticks by position, so many cores
  // don't all work on the same tick.
  public int tickOffset() {
    return Math.floorMod(worldPosition.hashCode(), RESCAN_INTERVAL);
  }

  public void markDirty() {
    dirty = true;
  }

  // A pooled block was removed, and a replacement at the same position gives an equal scan result,
  // so the next scan must rebuild the pools anyway.
  private void markPoolsStale() {
    dirty = true;
    poolsStale = true;
  }

  public ScanResult<BlockPos> lastScan() {
    return lastScan;
  }

  public @Nullable Multiblock multiblock() {
    return multiblock;
  }

  public @Nullable PowerPool power() {
    return power;
  }

  public @Nullable FertilizerPool fertilizer() {
    return fertilizer;
  }

  public @Nullable OutputSink outputs() {
    return outputs;
  }

  public @Nullable ResourceHandler<ItemResource> items() {
    return items;
  }

  public MeStatus meStatus() {
    return me == null || me.isRemoved() ? MeStatus.NONE : me.status();
  }

  public boolean allPartsLoaded() {
    return level != null
        && (multiblock == null || multiblock.all().stream().allMatch(level::isLoaded));
  }

  @Override
  public void onLoad() {
    super.onLoad();
    dirty = true;
  }

  private void scan(Level level) {
    dirty = false;
    boolean rebuild = poolsStale;
    poolsStale = false;
    ScanResult<BlockPos> result =
        StructureScanner.scan(
            worldPosition,
            pos -> Arrays.stream(Direction.values()).map(pos::relative).toList(),
            pos -> typeAt(level, pos),
            MPConfig.PART_CAP.get());
    if (result.equals(lastScan) && !rebuild) {
      return;
    }
    lastScan = result;
    if (result.problem() == Problem.WAITING_FOR_CHUNKS) {
      // The multiblock is kept so a structure with an unloaded part pauses instead of unforming,
      // while the pools are dropped so nothing touches a block entity in an unloaded chunk.
      power = null;
      fertilizer = null;
      outputs = null;
      me = null;
      items = null;
    } else {
      Multiblock previous = multiblock;
      multiblock = result.formed() ? Multiblock.from(result) : null;
      if (previous != null) {
        stopPlanters(
            level, previous.planters(), multiblock == null ? List.of() : multiblock.planters());
      }
      buildPools(level);
    }
    level.invalidateCapabilities(worldPosition);
    setChanged();
  }

  // No scan runs once the core is gone, so the core stops its planters here, or they would stay
  // ACTIVE and GROWING.
  @Override
  public void preRemoveSideEffects(BlockPos pos, BlockState state) {
    if (level != null && multiblock != null) {
      stopPlanters(level, multiblock.planters(), List.of());
    }
  }

  private static void stopPlanters(
      Level level, List<BlockPos> planters, List<BlockPos> stillFormed) {
    for (BlockPos pos : planters) {
      if (!stillFormed.contains(pos)
          && level.isLoaded(pos)
          && level.getBlockEntity(pos) instanceof PlanterBlockEntity planter) {
        planter.stopFromCore();
      }
    }
  }

  private void buildPools(Level level) {
    if (multiblock == null) {
      power = null;
      fertilizer = null;
      outputs = null;
      me = null;
      items = null;
      return;
    }
    power =
        new PowerPool(
            blockEntities(level, multiblock.power(), PowerBlockEntity.class), this::markPoolsStale);
    fertilizer =
        new FertilizerPool(
            blockEntities(level, multiblock.fertilizer(), FertilizerBlockEntity.class),
            this::markPoolsStale);
    BlockPos mePos = multiblock.me();
    me = mePos != null && level.getBlockEntity(mePos) instanceof MeLink link ? link : null;
    outputs =
        new OutputSink(
            blockEntities(level, multiblock.export(), ExportBlockEntity.class),
            me,
            this::markPoolsStale);
    items = DoorwayHandlers.items(fertilizer, outputs);
  }

  private static <T extends BlockEntity> List<T> blockEntities(
      Level level, List<BlockPos> positions, Class<T> type) {
    List<T> found = new ArrayList<>();
    for (BlockPos pos : positions) {
      BlockEntity blockEntity = level.getBlockEntity(pos);
      if (type.isInstance(blockEntity)) {
        found.add(type.cast(blockEntity));
      }
    }
    return found;
  }

  private static PartType typeAt(Level level, BlockPos pos) {
    if (!level.isLoaded(pos)) {
      return PartType.UNLOADED;
    }
    return level.getBlockState(pos).getBlock() instanceof PartBlock part
        ? part.partType()
        : PartType.NOT_A_PART;
  }
}
package io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.multiblock;

import io.github.julianperge.modular_planters.blockentity.CoreBlockEntity;
import net.neoforged.neoforge.transfer.CombinedResourceHandler;
import net.neoforged.neoforge.transfer.DelegatingResourceHandler;
import net.neoforged.neoforge.transfer.ResourceHandler;
import net.neoforged.neoforge.transfer.energy.EnergyHandler;
import net.neoforged.neoforge.transfer.item.ItemResource;
import org.jspecify.annotations.Nullable;

public final class DoorwayHandlers {
  private DoorwayHandlers() {}

  public static @Nullable EnergyHandler energy(CoreBlockEntity core) {
    PowerPool power = core.power();
    return power == null ? null : power.insertView();
  }

  public static @Nullable ResourceHandler<ItemResource> items(CoreBlockEntity core) {
    return core.items();
  }

  // The core builds this once each time it rebuilds its pools, and a removed fertilizer or export
  // block changes the slot count, so until that rebuild each call combines the views again.
  public static ResourceHandler<ItemResource> items(FertilizerPool fertilizer, OutputSink outputs) {
    ResourceHandler<ItemResource> whole =
        new CombinedResourceHandler<>(fertilizer.insertView(), outputs.extractView());
    return new DelegatingResourceHandler<>(
        () ->
            fertilizer.allLive() && outputs.allLive()
                ? whole
                : new CombinedResourceHandler<>(fertilizer.insertView(), outputs.extractView()));
  }
}
